<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:14:08Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israeli strikes kill four in Lebanon after alleged Hezbollah drone launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f092c7b5f51c788e024a04ac5e9f543b4ebc14bf865310817e33798dddffbcb</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:13:20Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T08:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260906-israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-lebanon-after-alleged-hezbollah-drone-launch--d3c0c1b9e0a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260906-israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-lebanon-after-alleged-hezbollah-drone-launch" /><summary type="html">Israeli air strikes on southern Lebanon Sunday killed four people, two of them women, the country's health ministry said. Israel's military said that the strikes were a response to an alleged Hezbollah drone launch targeting troops in the Israeli-occupied "security zone" in the country's south.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US ambassador to Israel visits Palestinian town hit by West Bank settler violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5c49175aa5071655f44f35a9570da6eaf91ed018f47e840ae8996f0f0e291ea</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:14:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-us-ambassador-to-israel-visits-palestinian-town-hit-by-west-bank-settler-violence--9088e5f15b75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-us-ambassador-to-israel-visits-palestinian-town-hit-by-west-bank-settler-violence" /><summary type="html">US ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee on Saturday visited Turmus Ayya, a Palestinian town in the Israeli-occupied West Bank that has been repeatedly targeted by Israeli settler violence. Huckabee, a staunch supporter of Israel and its illegal settlements in the Palestinian territory, said that it was in the Israeli government's interests to take action against violent settlers.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US military says it struck 3 Iranian oil tankers after missile attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48f2917a08742188ae3d92b72e69e185e9b0ee5f985af866567327f94bac30e9</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T05:01:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people--9a0ff2430b05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people" /><summary type="html">The US military said on Saturday it had struck and destroyed three Iranian oil tankers after Navy warships were targeted with missiles, adding that no American personnel ​were ​harmed. Earlier, Tehran accused the US of attacking an Iranian tanker near Kharg Island in the Persian Gulf, a key oil terminal. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b49685cee338bfd79bc0815fc780737992b945217e11732764fe8fe046fc1609</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T16:26:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says--03f625c09b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says" /><summary type="html">The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli army has seized Lebanon's key Ali al-Taher ridge from Hezbollah</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd24f61d62b0eeabfe88f6cd509c5f5685e8b88e43b3f6fa49a8f1ec4174be4</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:27:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah--71676c0b7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah" /><summary type="html">Israel has seized the strategically placed Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon from Hezbollah fighters, Defence Minister Israel Katz said Friday. The Iran-aligned Shiite group did not confirm losing the highland, which sits around 10 kilometres from the border with Israel and was pummelled by Israeli strikes in recent weeks despite a ceasefire.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>New fears of oil supply disruption as US-Iran hostilities resume</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:348948373838ff8703b95d7ab9950fcc706a5edc50c190abcecf33c09689df7d</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:56:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume--0869871bdd37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume" /><summary type="html">Renewed hostilities between the United States and Iran have brought back fears of oil supply disruption. Prices are on track for their steepest weekly gain since mid-July, up 7.6%, as the US-Iran war enters its seventh month. Twenty-five percent of the world's oil supply comes through the Strait of Hormuz, which has been blocked since the beginning of the war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle gives more details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says Iran war is 'small potatoes', Israel strikes southern Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fea1d30d28c3180949028e458bd50bd8fc34d9b882738a2a92ac9a2014d40e5e</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:56:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz--7d0e3110ee0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Friday said the Iran war was "small potatoes" for the US, a day after Vice President JD Vance said he wouldn't describe the conflict as a war. In Lebanon, an Israeli strike killed two people in the south, state media reported. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>No, UN chief Guterres did not call Francesca Albanese 'out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba208e548acbc36096c2a64f5bdcfc7ee404b278e39738329feec5800eca50db</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T19:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control--dd310962b9f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">Pro-Israel lobby group UN Watch has alleged that UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres referred to Francesca Albanese, the UN's Special Rapporteur on Palestine, as "out of control", saying he'd previously called her a "horrible woman". But Guterres named no one in his remarks. He said "many" independent rapporteurs were "totally out of control", without singling out any individual. The UN has since said that linking the comment specifically to Albanese is a "misreading" of his remarks. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f195089018ece131a59eb56b02e52fb4fd501e5aa82671126e5f1a17f690912a</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:00:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith--cf972620ce2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith" /><summary type="html">A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli attacks in West Bank at 'unprecedented' level, PNI leader Barghouti says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef5e9bf515686c4dcdc9d29a9c82f3586fcf1997e22b75320f98b8a5f317a524</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:26:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says--38c73f0a94fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, the secretary general of the Palestinian National Initiative (PNI) party Mustafa Barghouti said the level of Israeli attacks on Palestinians in the West Bank had become "totally unprecedented". With tensions escalating, activists accuse settlers of operating with total impunity. "Their goal is clear: it is ethnic cleansing," Barghouti stated, calling Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's reaction to the attacks hypocritical.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Has Iran modified its rocket systems to fire mines into the Strait of Hormuz?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23621f2d5913b0660606db4734a5c13fd0fced23bb2f076ba914b0bfb57d7b5</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T05:57:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz--d9050c0ecfa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Fighting escalated in the Middle East over the weekend after US airstrikes on Sunday targeted Iranian rocket launchers on the island of Larak. The exchange of fire was instigated by the US in retaliation against Iran’s new capabilities for firing mines from rockets into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran’s use of rocket launchers to deploy sea mines into the strategic waterway would be unprecedented, but not implausible. Even so, some analysts remain sceptical.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran hits US targets in Mideast, wedding strikes being probed, Vance says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ab34fec54fc1b4b9552cc89253eb379757c8d627d5ea0189757cf2e473fee43</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T05:19:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike--e1bf83f56bbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran said on Thursday it hit US military bases in Kuwait and the UAE in retaliation for a US strike on a wedding party that killed four people and injured nearly 70. While the US military has reiterated that it never targets civilians, Vice President JD Vance said the strike was being investigated.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Toppling Iran’s Islamic regime ‘within reach’, Netanyahu says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976ecaf97c152021ee720b547a65d83e8f10bebd8e56ed0b83655ace1b49f2bc</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:08:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran--67d09afbe2b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Thursday voiced confidence that Iran's Islamic republic could soon fall, saying it was weaker than ever. Earlier, Iran's army said it targeted US bases in the UAE and Kuwait. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4226e5cd12960ab095dc3a867ad4004e19abe8fb77de8a842ee50958a44cbc01</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T01:22:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike--7495f90c90eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5374938687be7ba398cc18b272966da4d1b83fb0018243b31554f9ee0aed8e23</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:57:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1--e29deba63932.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1" /><summary type="html">As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes resume, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, clips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Elsewhere, a 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli FM Gideon Sa'ar: 'I hope Iran will not make the mistake of attacking us'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:562af7af13541b3d4286f024d61dfc234e7a007c36774b579ea3ac154e493315</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:49:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us--4ec8673d7440.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260902-israeli-fm-gideon-sa-ar-i-hope-iran-will-not-make-the-mistake-of-attacking-us" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israel's Minister of Foreign Affairs Gideon Sa’ar addressed the resumption in fighting between the US and Iran, and warned that any Iranian attack on Israel would trigger a "severe" response. He also accused Tehran of continuing to pursue "nuclear weapons aspirations", claiming that Israel "will not allow" Iran to achieve them.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Videos and debris raise questions over alleged US strike on Iranian wedding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6db856b05415a4dfc58f64045086cd8b7f72835de1a0ad222eeccfdac1d406c</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T17:31:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding--89b2ba4b7915.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-videos-and-debris-raise-questions-over-alleged-us-strike-on-iranian-wedding" /><summary type="html">On the evening of September 1, a barrage of US missile and drone attacks on a town in southern Iran allegedly struck a wedding ceremony, killing at least five people, including a four-year-old boy. FRANCE 24 geolocated a direct hit to the civilian building where local residents say the wedding was being held. The building was more than 135 meters from the apparent target, a communications tower.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel ‘organised and prepared’ to remove Gaza population if US gives green light, Katz says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c33f6236685d177eff99d24dcc958d1a14a4f7e53c82e6a511af5ae24de9bba</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:56:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz--8521b89aab45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-israel-organised-and-prepared-to-remove-gaza-population-if-us-gives-green-light-katz" /><summary type="html">Israel is "organised and prepared" to remove Palestininians from Gaza "by every way possible", Defence Minister Israel Katz told reporters Wednesday, adding that there was no alternative "solution" to crisis. The Israeli government was simply waiting for the US to figure out where to take the displaced Gazans, he said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Xi calls on Mideast nations to be ‘masters of their own affairs’ in rare Egypt visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24906c53ca5d0c906c596fd9ec278bc33439d1edcd3d052b7a90cbdc4b35b419</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:22:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit--a27043953780.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-xi-calls-on-mideast-nations-to-be-masters-of-their-own-affairs-in-rare-egypt-visit" /><summary type="html">Chinese President Xi Jinping on Wednesday called on "the people of the Middle East" to oppose "externalinterference" and consider reshaping the region's security order during a visit to Egypt. The rare visit by the Chinese leader comes as Beijing aims to expand its influence in the region as the Iran war tests the reliability of the traditional US security umbrella in a vital geostrategic zone.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UNIFIL peacekeepers patrol south Lebanon, caught between Israel and Hezbollah</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a17dbd4d34941cfbb4475bc8c6b1d14c14abf71913c32442f2a950e9c87499</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:41:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260902-unifil-peacekeepers-patrol-south-lebanon-caught-between-israel-and-hezbollah--b0682915af5a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260902-unifil-peacekeepers-patrol-south-lebanon-caught-between-israel-and-hezbollah" /><summary type="html">Since this spring, about 6 percent of Lebanon has been occupied by the Israeli army. On the ground, around 600 French soldiers from the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) continue to patrol the zone. The delicate peacekeeping mission documents violations of UN resolutions by both Israel and Hezbollah, with its own future highly uncertain. Our France 2 colleagues report, with FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Iran: US accused of hitting wedding party in latest strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9fca6a3ee525ac3e7cfa91d2e6182855ec395403142efb6c02f90a2f751ab8b4</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T11:11:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes--5e3776f2d927.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes" /><summary type="html">#Tehran says at least four people were killed and dozens more wounded in a #US strike on a town near in the south of #Iran, near the Strait of #Hormuz.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says prepared to resume strikes on Iran at 'any time'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4eab5d3c57a340b85bfae0c59744a88c19227f651a64416927125e2d699a1ea</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:38:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping--2a2323f6d3bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260902-us-military-striking-targets-in-iran-after-attempted-attacks-on-shipping" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Wednesday suggested he was ready to strike Iran again “at any time" after he proposed renaming the Strait of Hormuz the “Trump Strait.” Earlier, Iran had attacked US military bases in the Gulf following another round of US airstrikes on Iranian soil. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US and Iran trade fire as hostilities flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8635a20c88285199abc106ecadf855ca65efff29778e083c0e48fc10c51fbfc</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:15:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-us-and-iran-trade-fire-as-hostilities-flare-again--37e010d049e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-us-and-iran-trade-fire-as-hostilities-flare-again" /><summary type="html">The US military hit targets in Iran on Tuesday as Tehran reponded with retaliatory strikes as hostilities between the two countries flared once again in an intermittent war that has lasted more than six months. One US strike hit a home hosting a wedding, killing four people and wounding dozens, local officials said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>A Hezbollah hideout stuffed with cash? Nope, this video was AI-generated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72d5630caffda638af8571a60468dda7386edf11b9d1c37ac27666879535e85b</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:01:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated--9c252e98ffac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-hezbollah-hideout-stuffed-cash-ai-generated" /><summary type="html">A number of pro-Israel social media accounts have shared a video they claim shows wads of cash and stacks of gold bars in a cache belonging to a deceased Hezbollah leader. There's only one issue: the footage was created using AI. The original video was shared by an Egyptian satirical site.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu's wife shares conspiracy claim that opposition leader knew of Oct 7 attacks in advance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fbe1d51cb5eaebc7c211bd383e0143d419ed6561f3ad146af4c43f215e50dd2</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T09:36:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-atta--a964727714fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-netanyahu-s-wife-shares-conspiracy-that-opposition-leader-had-early-knowledge-of-oct-7-attacks" /><summary type="html">As Israel prepares for what are expected to be close-fought parliamentary elections in October, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's wife Sara on Monday shared a conspiracy theory that centre-left opposition figure Yair Golan had advance warning of the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US military striking targets in Iran after attempted attacks on shipping</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e9ec657983fa00dbcd976b1d046b0797ef4ef607ca2185f4cc4e8c85a84561b</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T03:38:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again--805a2484da57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again" /><summary type="html">The US military said on Tuesday it is striking new targets in Iran as hostilities flare again after a month without military action. US Central Command said that the strikes follow recent attempted attacks by the Iranian government against commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c17b672b518187c844e017b262f2a61fc4bfb0a712e3c22221bf2d9972e54ea</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:36:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull--926c2ca9c70e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47c8bf7c4ac6f7736c2333f270d379cbfeea0e1875f2581937bbeeac116eadac</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T18:37:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks--7701c0e7ac56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e57bdb4731ce3eba1cab67e6854715a53365a92a25422cc52ba6d1d8224db785</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T16:54:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt--b62ae1447324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt" /><summary type="html">A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e72b6d549489ed9bf56347cd1f540188e50b2e0497210bdd99b8828bf57b8b71</id><updated>2026-09-06T12:12:07Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:33:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end--9f77617ac27c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.</summary></entry></feed>
